{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013o99YCeeafKyfGShzYX3Bz","type":"tool_result","content":"29:  const cfgP = G.quickMatchCfg({ seed: 11 }); cfgP.difficulty = 'Easy'; startCfg(G, game, cfgP); G.M.perfectPlayer = true; G.M.cpuControl = true; const IP = runMatch(G, game, G.M);\nFAIL match › Lucky Seven fires on Sonny's next attack, once: {\"armedSpikes\":0,\"fired\":0,\"cords\":0}\n48 passed, 1 failed (ai, match) in 16 s","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8aedb0d-fc32-4598-b2c3-8a34e0c85184","uuid":"d5befdd1-8bc0-42b2-bcc1-a59dd98147e5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:13:02.268Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"29:  const cfgP = G.quickMatchCfg({ seed: 11 }); cfgP.difficulty = 'Easy'; startCfg(G, game, cfgP); G.M.perfectPlayer = true; G.M.cpuControl = true; const IP = runMatch(G, game, G.M);\nFAIL match › Lucky Seven fires on Sonny's next attack, once: {\"armedSpikes\":0,\"fired\":0,\"cords\":0}\n48 passed, 1 failed (ai, match) in 16 s","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-215911__x5b1962/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2394,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2394,"newLines":16,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"5fdadd0d-6524-4558-9af2-079b7bb58d23\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":195,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":145,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"cd6b80fe-2564-4447-a6a5-85435100be88\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghUNAq4fWMb1UWCTp36F\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":483,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":868596,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":483},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"f65e7df7-c517-473b-9989-22ab3d181fe4\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:12:37.515Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CghUNATW8nwqdvpXfv3Kt\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":6136,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghUNAq4fWMb1UWCTp36F\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I re-ran the scripted playthrough and the Quilting Bee suite in full on the current code, after the last game and test changes, and all 83 checks passed. The full suite at that point was 341 passed, 0 failed, including the AI Hub harness's four browser scenarios.\\n\\n**Evidence for each point:**\\n- **Playthrough end to end:** all 68 checks pass in one clean run, with no failures from the AI player and no errors. The story goes New Game → M1 to M14 → results → credits → free play, plus side quests S1, S2 and S3, and the final \\\"every quest is done\\\" check passes. That includes M13 (Mortimer starts the siege, all three waves survived) and M14 (Gnarlgrim tangled and defeated, Chapter One clear, town level 5).\\n- **Quilting Bee, all 15 checks:**\\n  - The barn scales with the number of players.\\n  - The round goes countdown → build → raid.\\n  - Barn blocks score +3 each, and kills score for the player.\\n  - Surviving the raid ends the round as a win; the Banner falling ends it as a loss.\\n  - Standings list every player once; the awards include Master Quilter and the Knot Cutter (the player with the most kills).\\n  - The game returns to the title after a solo round.\\n- **TODO, FIXME, XXX, placeholder, stub, \\\"not implemented\\\":** a case-insensitive search of all 54 files in `src`, `tests` and `tools` returned no matches (exit status 1).\\n- **Usage:** TASK.md asks for cost, tokens and session time only if estimates are available. This session doesn't expose token or billing counts to me, so the field stays \\\"unknown\\\" rather than a guess.\\n\\nThe game file and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder; the exit interview parses with no empty fields.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 21:59:11\\n- **Source:** Dragon Quest Builders\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** a sandbox action RPG (block building, crafting, town building, real-time combat, a siege and bosses), seen in third-person isometric 2.5D over a true voxel world. The camera turns in 90° steps and zooms; a three-quarter view is a setting.\\n- **Tech:**\\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, lightly modified, plus my own voxel world, renderer, physics and pathfinding, in plain ES2020 JavaScript on Canvas 2D and Web Audio.\\n  - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (client session.js 1.4.0).\\n  - Node 18+ for the headless tests and Playwright 1.63.0 for the browser checks.\\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel style with an original patchwork-quilt look: every block a stitched fabric patch, felt menu panels with running-stitch borders, a patchwork logo.\\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs and moves, plus new moves (place, eat, stir, chop), poses, tools drawn on the rig, boss wind-ups, swinging doors, a fluttering banner, portal swirls and an unravel effect.\\n- **Audio:** all in code: 14 original songs on a leitmotif (the town waltz gains layers as the town levels up), 12 jingles, about 50 synthesized sound effects, and Animalese voices for each character with their own Voices volume setting.\\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for the Quilting Bee co-op round: the game's own card, a host-run world, standings, awards, time-up, leave, end and server mode. The same round plays solo with bots outside the hub.\\n- **Testing:** headless scripted tests in 19 suites (341 checks), including the full playthrough and a fake multi-copy hub with latency and loss; Playwright screenshots; the hub harness's four scenarios.\\n- **Research:** no web research on the source game. I read the engine's documentation and source sections, and the AI Hub protocol README.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** unknown\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 41: 31 bugs in the game and its AI player, and 10 mistakes in the tests themselves.\\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 8: the Quilters' Hall not forming (blocks quest M10), damaged blocks healing between hits, Gnarlgrim falling into the void, any hit knocking the player off the ballista, no results screen after a skipped finale, invisible monsters for co-op clients, the player hidden in the opening area, and silenced audio after the attract mode.\\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough from New Game to Chapter Clear. It found the block-healing, ballista, siege and finale bugs.\\n4. **Least helpful test:** the world-generation determinism check, which never failed.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n1. **What I liked most:** the views are exact linear projections, so a voxel renderer plugged straight into the engine's depth-sorted queue, x-ray, lighting and particles. The rigs, dialog, menus, saves and settings came free.\\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. Wall items need a screen box for the x-ray pass, which I only found in the source. The default isometric view's block height isn't a whole number of pixels, so I made my own views.\\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** the voxel world: storage, a renderer with cutaway and water, body physics with stairs, and pathfinding.\\n4. **Hardest part of the engine:** depth-sorting real 3D blocks in a 2D painter's queue designed for heightmap walls.\\n5. **What I changed in the engine, and why** (each change marked `// DQB:`):\\n   - A mouse-wheel accessor that works while the camera wheel is off, so the wheel can cycle the hotbar.\\n   - A right-stick flick for 90° camera turns.\\n   - A per-letter dialog hook for the voices.\\n   - A separate Voices audio bus.\\n   - Three tools drawn on the character rig: a darning stick, a cobble club and the Seam Ripper.\\n6. **One thing I would change:** a built-in voxel map type with its own depth-lift hook and occluder boxes.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n1. **What I liked most:** the clear definition of done and the detailed plan. The controller-first, 10-foot rules made UI decisions easy.\\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan's file names used another model and timestamp than TASK.md's.\\n3. **Hardest thing to do:** proving the whole chapter completes through real triggers, while also building netcode and an attract mode.\\n4. **What I would change:** a smaller slice or staged delivery. The scope is very large for one pass.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":483,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":868596,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":483},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"9c2cacab-d062-43aa-854a-b5b7385f0f34\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:12:47.633Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CghUNATW8nwqdvpXfv3Kt\"}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: Not satisfied on transcript evidence. The bundled HTML was rebuilt and exit-interview.json parses with no empty fields, and the final reply contains all four sections. But TASK.md's Usage field is left as 'unknown' with no estimate attempted, and TASK.md asks for estimates when available. Also, the transcript never shows the TASK.md-listed 'Testing' parameters or the Testing claim of 'no errors' at the final state being verified by the final full run including browser checks after the last edits; the last full run cited is 341 passed after an exit-interview rewrite, and the playthrough was re-run in a separate pass. More importantly, the self-declared 'every feature implemented' rests on a test suite and an assertion-only check, with several TASK.md items (for example the In-game About/Credits content, touch-only notice, and the Dev-mode stamp round trip) having only partial or indirect verification in the transcript, so completion of every feature is not clearly established.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"35f00df7-cf08-4419-8394-92e63e27b545\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:12:50.162Z\",\"isSynthetic\":true}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"b73f3efd-7d2c-4835-b19e-fd82b3113953\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":228,\"estimated_token