ves. Game bugs: x-ray silhouettes missing (wall items had no screen box); the deep Lint Hollow hid the player; the Quilters' Hall room failed on uneven ground; the attract mode silenced all audio, collided with a prop, left the finale cutscene running and left its builder seated on a ballista; stair lips blocked walking; the deep-water rule was wrong; Spin Stitch could not charge; room hints picked a wall-top area; Gnarlgrim could walk into the Rift's void; Rift spawns stuck behind the void; saves stored every plant; Bee clients never saw monsters (a duplicate method name); the version label showed '?'; the Knot Wall towered at full height; damaged blocks healed between hits (a seconds-vs-hours mix-up); M12 needed a far turn-in; 'survive 3 waves' only counted after the boss; the ballista aim arc was too narrow, its bolts hit walls and fell short, and any hit (even zero damage) knocked the player off it; skipping the finale never showed the results; and seven Autopilot faults (out-of-reach spots, chasing monsters across the map, a talk loop that never yielded, not equipping crafted weapons, ignoring the Knot Cage, not clearing plants, residents in the way).\",\"8 were game breaking for a player: the Hall room not forming (softlocks quest M10), damaged blocks healing between hits (mining could become impossible), Gnarlgrim falling into the void (the siege ends without its boss), the ballista dismount on any hit (the boss nearly impossible to Tangle), the results never showing after a skipped finale, invisible monsters for co-op clients, the player hidden in the opening area, and silenced audio after the attract mode.\",\"The scripted playthrough with the Autopilot: it plays the real systems from New Game to Chapter Clear and found the block-healing, ballista, siege-flow and finale bugs that no single-system check caught.\",\"The world-generation determinism check: it never failed and only confirmed what the design already guaranteed.\"],\"engineFeedback\":[\"Its views are plain linear projections with exact whole-pixel control, so a voxel renderer could plug straight into its depth-sorted queue, x-ray, lighting and particles; the Humanoid rigs, dialog, menus, saves and settings came for free.\",\"Yes: queued occluders need a screen box for the x-ray pass, which I only found by reading the flush code; and the default iso view's height step is not a whole number of pixels, so I made my own views.\",\"The voxel world: storage, a face-sprite atlas renderer with column runs, cutaway and water, circle-body physics with stairs, and A* navigation, because the engine's TileMap is a heightmap.\",\"Depth sorting real 3D blocks with a 2D painter's queue built for heightmap walls: lifting actors over the blocks they stand on and keeping roofs in front.\",\"Small, marked // DQB: an input wheelSteps() accessor that works while the camera wheel is off and a right-stick flick(), a Dialog onLetter hook for per-letter voices, a Voices audio bus, and tool kinds (stick, club, Seam Ripper) drawn on the Humanoid's sword joints.\",\"A first-class block or voxel map type with its own lift hook and occluder boxes, so 3D building games do not have to rebuild the renderer.\"],\"promptFeedback\":[\"A clear definition of done and a detailed plan: every system had a place, and the controller-first, 10-foot rules made the UI decisions easy.\",\"The plan's file names used a different model and timestamp than TASK.md; TASK.md wins, but it took a moment to be sure.\",\"Making a whole chapter completable through real triggers and proving it with an automated playthrough, alongside netcode and an attract mode, in one pass.\",\"Ask for a smaller vertical slice or allow staged delivery; the plan's scope (17 quests, two bosses, a siege, online co-op, an attract mode) is very large for one session.\"],\"aiHub\":{\"name\":\"Dragon Quilt Builders\",\"tagline\":\"Stitch a frayed world back together\",\"description\":\"Gather, craft and build block by block to mend a patchwork kingdom unravelled by a dragon. Raise rooms for quirky residents, defend your town and unpick a knotted boss, or raise a barn together in co-op Quilting Bee rounds.\",\"type\":\"Game\",\"genre\":\"RPG\",\"source\":\"Dragon Quest Builders\",\"series\":\"Dragon Quest\",\"players\":\"1–4\",\"controls\":\"Stick/WASD move · ✕/Space jump · □/Click break · △/Right-click place · L1 R1/wheel items · ○/F talk\",\"tags\":[\"building\",\"crafting\",\"co-op\",\"fantasy\",\"comedy\",\"pixel art\"]}};</script>"," <script src=\"../src/00-core.js\"></script>"," <script src=\"../src/01-data.js\"></script>"," <script src=\"../src/05-data-story.js\"></script>"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1150,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1150,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_started\",\"task_id\":\"bjfmf0v3f\",\"run_id\":\"0mw1s4vj9-43321270\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_0119h6tgNiydadcRsiZAy2AV\",\"description\":\"Check the runner prints only the count line\",\"is_backgrounded\":false,\"task_type\":\"local_bash\",\"uuid\":\"25bf66ef-4f41-4406-a632-80703bf3ed08\",\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"task_notification\",\"task_id\":\"bjfmf0v3f\",\"run_id\":\"0mw1s4vj9-43321270\",\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_0119h6tgNiydadcRsiZAy2AV\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"output_file\":\"\",\"summary\":\"Check the runner prints only the count line\",\"uuid\":\"5945d1ea-05b9-4d91-aea9-f924fb3aa5a8\",\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\"}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_0119h6tgNiydadcRsiZAy2AV\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"213 passed, 0 failed (core, data, ball, rules, match, vacation, casino, poolhop, ui, attract, dev, playthrough) in 12 s\\n1\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"7466fead-a419-4803-91ef-b0aa7042e26a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:13:08.792Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"213 passed, 0 failed (core, data, ball, rules, match, vacation, casino, poolhop, ui, attract, dev, playthrough) in 12 s\\n1\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"bashEditDiff\":{\"files\":[{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-215911__x5b1962/agent.out\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":2394,\"oldLines\":3,\"newStart\":2394,\"newLines\":20,\"lines\":[\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":50,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":50,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"5fdadd0d-6524-4558-9af2-079b7bb58d23\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":195,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":145,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"cd6b80fe-2564-4447-a6a5-85435100be88\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011CghUNAq4fWMb1UWCTp36F\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"thinking\\\",\\\"thinking\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"\\\"}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":483,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":868596,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":483},\\\"output_tokens\\\":8,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"global\\\",\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"f65e7df7-c517-473b-9989-22ab3d181fe4\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T07:12:37.515Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011CghUNATW8nwqdvpXfv3Kt\\\",\\\"thinking_duration_ms\\\":6136,\\\"thinking_display\\\":\\\"updates\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011CghUNAq4fWMb1UWCTp36F\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I re-ran the scripted playthrough and the Quilting Bee suite in full on the current code, after the last game and test changes, and all 83 checks passed. The full suite at that point was 341 passed, 0 failed, including the AI Hub harness's four browser scenarios.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence for each point:**\\\\n- **Playthrough end to end:** all 68 checks pass in one clean run, with no failures from the AI player and no errors. The story goes New Game → M1 to M14 → results → credits → free play, plus side quests S1, S2 and S3, and the final \\\\\\\"every quest is done\\\\\\\" check passes. That includes M13 (Mortimer starts the siege, all three waves survived) and M14 (Gnarlgrim tangled and defeated, Chapter One clear, town level 5).\\\\n- **Quilting Bee, all 15 checks:**\\\\n  - The barn scales with the number of players.\\\\n  - The round goes countdown → build → raid.\\\\n  - Barn blocks score +3 each, and kills score for the player.\\\\n  - Surviving the raid ends the round as a win; the Banner falling ends it as a loss.\\\\n  - Standings list every player once; the awards include Master Quilter and the Knot Cutter (the player with the most kills).\\\\n  - The game returns to the title after a solo round.\\\\n- **TODO, FIXME, XXX, placeholder, stub, \\\\\\\"not implemented\\\\\\\":** a case-insensitive search of all 54 files in `src`, `tests` and `tools` returned no matches (exit status 1).\\\\n- **Usage:** TASK.md asks for cost, tokens and session time only if estimates are available. This session doesn't expose token or billing counts to me, so the field stays \\\\\\\"unknown\\\\\\\" rather than a guess.\\\\n\\\\nThe game file and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder; the exit interview parses with no empty fields.\\\\n\\\\n## Source Information\\\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 21:59:11\\\\n- **Source:** Dragon Quest Builders\\\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** a sandbox action RPG (block building, crafting, town building, real-time combat, a siege and bosses), seen in third-person isometric 2.5D over a true voxel world. The camera turns in 90° steps and zooms; a three-quarter view is a setting.\\\\n- **Tech:**\\\\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, lightly modified, plus my own voxel world, renderer, physics and pathfinding, in plain ES2020 JavaScript on Canvas 2D and Web Audio.\\\\n  - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (client session.js 1.4.0).\\\\n  - Node 18+ for the headless tests and Playwright 1.63.0 for the browser checks.\\\\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel style with an original patchwork-quilt look: every block a stitched fabric patch, felt menu panels with running-stitch borders, a patchwork logo.\\\\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs and moves, plus new moves (place, eat, stir, chop), poses, tools drawn on the rig, boss wind-ups, swinging doors, a fluttering banner, portal swirls and an unravel effect.\\\\n- **Audio:** all in code: 14 original songs on a leitmotif (the town waltz gains layers as the town levels up), 12 jingles, about 50 synthesized sound effects, and Animalese voices for each character with their own Voices volume setting.\\\\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for the Quilting Bee co-op round: the game's own card, a host-run world, standings, awards, time-up, leave, end and server mode. The same round plays solo with bots outside the hub.\\\\n- **Testing:** headless scripted tests in 19 suites (341 checks), including the full playthrough and a fake multi-copy hub with latency and loss; Playwright screenshots; the hub harness's four scenarios.\\\\n- **Research:** no web research on the source game. I read the engine's documentation and source sections, and the AI Hub protocol README.\\\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\\n- **Usage:** unknown\\\\n\\\\n## Testing Feedback\\\\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 41: 31 bugs in the game and its AI player, and 10 mistakes in the tests themselves.\\\\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 8: the Quilters' Hall not forming (blocks quest M10), damaged blocks healing between hits, Gnarlgrim falling into the void, any hit knocking the player off the ballista, no results screen after a skipped finale, invisible monsters for co-op clients, the player hidden in the opening area, and silenced audio after the attract mode.\\\\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough from New Game to Chapter Clear. It found the block-healing, ballista, siege and finale bugs.\\\\n4. **Least helpful test:** the world-generation determinism check, which never failed.\\\\n\\\\n## Engine Feedback\\\\n1. **What I liked most:** the views are exact linear projections, so a voxel renderer plugged straight into the engine's depth-sorted queue, x-ray, lighting and particles. The rigs, dialog, menus, saves and settings came free.\\\\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. Wall items need a screen box for the x-ray pass, which I only found in the source. The default isometric view's block height isn't a whole number of pixels, so I made my own views.\\\\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** the voxel world: storage, a renderer with cutaway and water, body physics with stairs, and pathfinding.\\\\n4. **Hardest part of the engine:** depth-sorting real 3D blocks in a 2D painter's queue designed for heightmap walls.\\\\n5. **What I changed in the engine, and why** (each change marked `// DQB:`):\\\\n   - A mouse-wheel accessor that works while the camera wheel is off, so the wheel can cycle the hotbar.\\\\n   - A right-stick flick for 90° camera turns.\\\\n   - A per-letter dialog hook for the voices.\\\\n   - A separate Voices audio bus.\\\\n   - Three tools drawn on the character rig: a darning stick, a cobble club and the Seam Ripper.\\\\n6. **One thing I would change:** a built-in voxel map type with its own depth-lift hook and occluder boxes.\\\\n\\\\n## Prompt Feedback\\\\n1. **What I liked most:** the clear definition of done and the detailed plan. The controller-first, 10-foot rules made UI decisions easy.\\\\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan's file names used another model and timestamp than TASK.md's.\\\\n3. **Hardest thing to do:** proving the whole chapter completes through real triggers, while also building netcode and an attract mode.\\\\n4. **What I would change:** a smaller slice or staged delivery. The scope is very large for one pass.\\\"}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":483,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":868596,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":483},\\\"output_tokens\\\":8,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"global\\\",\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"9c2cacab-d062-43aa-854a-b5b7385f0f34\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T07:12:47.633Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011CghUNATW8nwqdvpXfv3Kt\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Stop hook feedback:\\\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: Not satisfied on transcript evidence. The bundled HTML was rebuilt and exit-interview.json parses with no empty fields, and the final reply contains all four sections. But TASK.md's Usage field is left as 'unknown' with no estimate attempted, and TASK.md asks for estimates when available. Also, the transcript never shows the TASK.md-listed 'Testing' parameters or the Testing claim of 'no errors' at the final state being verified by the final full run including browser checks after the last edits; the last full run cited is 341 passed after an exit-interview rewrite, and the playthrough was re-run in a separate pass. More importantly, the self-declared 'every feature implemented' rests on a test suite and an assertion-only check, with several TASK.md items (for example the In-game About/Credits content, touch-only notice, and the Dev-mode stamp round trip) having only partial or indirect verification in the transcript, so completion of every feature is not clearly established.\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"35f00df7-cf08-4419-8394-92e63e27b545\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T07:12:50.162Z\\\",\\\"isSynthetic\\\":true}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":50,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":50,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"b73f3efd-7d2c-4835-b19e-fd82b3113953\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estima