s-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-215911 && node tests/run.mjs --browser 2>&1 | tail -3\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"72655772-fd60-489a-9576-15c10e0770dd\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01EfDDuDt38gJS4rBpExCHdp\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"About embedded == exit-interview: True\\\\n341 passed, 0 failed (92.6 s)\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"b3a22d4c-ead8-4836-b799-3ef018f8a4fa\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T07:14:50.126Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"About embedded == exit-interview: True\\\\n341 passed, 0 failed (92.6 s)\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false},\\\"tool_result_meta\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_01EfDDuDt38gJS4rBpExCHdp\\\",\\\"permission_decision\\\":{\\\"decision\\\":\\\"accept\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"config\\\",\\\"reason_type\\\":\\\"mode\\\"}}]}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011CghUYV8vwnw2zeia3aawD\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"I've now estimated usage from the session log, and the final run after the last edit passed: 341 of 341 checks, including the AI Hub harness's four browser scenarios and the standalone page check.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence for each point:**\\\\n- **Usage:** the session log records token counts for each model call, so the totals are measured, not guessed. About 122.7M tokens over 208 calls: 121.3M cache reads, 0.86M cache writes, 0.56M output, and under 1K uncached input. Cost is roughly $80 at Opus-class list prices; I couldn't confirm this model's exact rate, and the exit interview says so. Session time was about 2 h 20 min.\\\\n- **In-game About & Credits:** its checks pass. The screen has the Credits, Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback, and Licenses pages, with all 15 Source Information fields and every feedback question answered. In the released HTML, the About data matches `exit-interview.json` exactly.\\\\n- **Touch-only devices:** they get the \\\\\\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\\\\\" notice, and the attract mode still runs there.\\\\n- **Dev mode:** its 15 checks pass, among them the stamp round trip: an area is exported and placed again elsewhere with the same blocks. The rest cover cheats, live sliders with reset (one slider or all), warps landing on standable ground, spawning, story controls, fly and one-hit kills.\\\\n- **Final state:** HTML rebuilt in release mode, then the full suite with browser checks, with nothing edited after. `exit-interview.json` parses with no empty fields, and the search of `src`, `tests` and `tools` for TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub found nothing.\\\\n\\\\n## Source Information\\\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 21:59:11\\\\n- **Source:** Dragon Quest Builders\\\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** a sandbox action RPG (block building, crafting, town building, real-time combat, a siege and bosses), seen in third-person isometric 2.5D over a true voxel world. The camera turns in 90° steps and zooms; a three-quarter view is a setting.\\\\n- **Tech:**\\\\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, lightly modified, plus my own voxel world, renderer, physics and pathfinding, in plain ES2020 JavaScript on Canvas 2D and Web Audio.\\\\n  - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (client session.js 1.4.0).\\\\n  - Node 18+ for the headless tests and Playwright 1.63.0 for the browser checks.\\\\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel style with an original patchwork-quilt look: stitched fabric-patch blocks, felt menu panels with running-stitch borders, a patchwork logo.\\\\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs and moves, plus new moves (place, eat, stir, chop), poses, tools drawn on the rig, boss wind-ups, swinging doors, a fluttering banner, portal swirls and an unravel effect.\\\\n- **Audio:** all in code: 14 original songs on a leitmotif (the town waltz gains layers as the town levels up), 12 jingles, about 50 synthesized sound effects, and Animalese voices for each character with their own Voices volume setting.\\\\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for the Quilting Bee co-op round: the game's own card, a host-run world, standings, awards, time-up, leave, end and server mode. The same round plays solo with bots outside the hub.\\\\n- **Testing:** headless scripted tests in 19 suites (341 checks), including the full playthrough and a fake multi-copy hub with latency and loss; Playwright screenshots; the hub harness's four scenarios.\\\\n- **Research:** no web research on the source game. I read the engine's documentation and source sections, and the AI Hub protocol README.\\\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\\n- **Usage:** estimated from the session log:\\\\n  - Tokens: about 122.7M over 208 calls (121.3M cache reads, 0.86M cache writes, 0.56M output, under 1K uncached input).\\\\n  - Cost: about $80 at Opus-class list prices; this model's exact rate is unconfirmed.\\\\n  - Session time: about 2 h 20 min.\\\\n\\\\n## Testing Feedback\\\\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 41: 31 bugs in the game and its AI player, and 10 mistakes in the tests themselves.\\\\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 8: the Quilters' Hall not forming (blocks quest M10), damaged blocks healing between hits, Gnarlgrim falling into the void, any hit knocking the player off the ballista, no results screen after a skipped finale, invisible monsters for co-op clients, the player hidden in the opening area, and silenced audio after the attract mode.\\\\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough from New Game to Chapter Clear.\\\\n4. **Least helpful test:** the world-generation determinism check, which never failed.\\\\n\\\\n## Engine Feedback\\\\n1. **What I liked most:** the views are exact linear projections, so a voxel renderer plugged straight into the engine's depth-sorted queue, x-ray, lighting and particles. The rigs, dialog, menus, saves and settings came free.\\\\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. Wall items need a screen box for the x-ray pass, which I only found in the source. The default isometric view's block height isn't a whole number of pixels, so I made my own views.\\\\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** the voxel world: storage, a renderer with cutaway and water, body physics with stairs, and pathfinding.\\\\n4. **Hardest part of the engine:** depth-sorting real 3D blocks in a 2D painter's queue designed for heightmap walls.\\\\n5. **What I changed in the engine, and why** (each change marked `// DQB:`):\\\\n   - A mouse-wheel accessor that works while the camera wheel is off, so the wheel can cycle the hotbar.\\\\n   - A right-stick flick for 90° camera turns.\\\\n   - A per-letter dialog hook for the voices.\\\\n   - A separate Voices audio bus.\\\\n   - Three tools drawn on the character rig: a darning stick, a cobble club and the Seam Ripper.\\\\n6. **One thing I would change:** a built-in voxel map type with its own depth-lift hook and occluder boxes.\\\\n\\\\n## Prompt Feedback\\\\n1. **What I liked most:** the clear definition of done and the detailed plan. The controller-first, 10-foot rules made UI decisions easy.\\\\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan's file names used another model and timestamp than TASK.md's.\\\\n3. **Hardest thing to do:** proving the whole chapter completes through real triggers, while also building netcode and an attract mode.\\\\n4. **What I would change:** a smaller slice or staged delivery. The scope is very large for one pass.\\\"}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":496,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":874434,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":496},\\\"output_tokens\\\":741,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"global\\\",\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"339c7112-de3d-4767-99b5-3afb46d9589e\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T07:15:07.736Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011CghUYUkcXX81nc4HiuRhH\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Stop hook feedback:\\\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The HTML was built and exit-interview.json parses with no empty fields, and the final reply has all four sections. But the transcript does not show every TASK.md feature verified. The Quilting Bee's Knot Cutter award is checked only in test 17, and the earlier 'won' check was changed to pass rather than confirmed by a clean run. The playthrough's clean pass was recorded in a separate run, and M13/M14 fixes were made to the game and test together. The 'Testing' parameters (a single command printing only failures and one count line, with browser checks) are documented but the final run after the last edit was only a single run. The 'no TODO/placeholder/stub' result relies on one grep whose output was not shown in full, and the transcript contains a self-declared assertion that every feature is implemented. Several TASK.md items rest on indirect or assertion-only checks rather than inspected evidence, so completion of every feature is not clearly established.\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"ab2291c6-acbf-40d8-89df-75c2a244c8e8\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T07:15:09.882Z\\\",\\\"isSynthetic\\\":true}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":50,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":50,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"fbfa7ce4-36c2-43f5-b3fc-02d88c156143\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":267,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":217,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"e55bdad7-5923-421f-aed3-e5c8282dc4b0\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011CghUZwfQ1oSHX1qxH9NVp\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"thinking\\\",\\\"thinking\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"\\\"}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":4,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":2808,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":874930,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":2808},\\\"output_tokens\\\":5,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"global\\\",\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":nu