{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D4FnXnHAre3XCHug57x4ra","type":"tool_result","content":"import { chromium } from 'playwright';\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\nconst dir = process.argv[2];\nconst srv = spawn('python3', ['-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], { cwd: dir, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\nconst port = await new Promise(res => { let b = ''; const on = d => { b += d; const m = /port (\\d+)/.exec(b); if (m) res(+m[1]); }; srv.stdout.on('data', on); srv.stderr.on('data', on); });\nconst br = await chromium.launch(), p = await br.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1400, height: 900 } });\nawait p.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/harness.html?game=game.html&players=2`); await p.waitForTimeout(6000);\nawait p.screenshot({ path: 'test-output/hub-card.png' });\nawait br.close(); srv.kill('SIGTERM'); console.log('ok', !!el);\nfile:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453/.tmp/card.mjs:9\nawait br.close(); srv.kill('SIGTERM'); console.log('ok', !!el);\n                                                           ^\n\nReferenceError: el is not defined","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8aedb0d-fc32-4598-b2c3-8a34e0c85184","uuid":"cb94e1c3-fcf8-4443-861e-e36290607d4c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:47:05.889Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"import { chromium } from 'playwright';\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\nconst dir = process.argv[2];\nconst srv = spawn('python3', ['-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], { cwd: dir, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });\nconst port = await new Promise(res => { let b = ''; const on = d => { b += d; const m = /port (\\d+)/.exec(b); if (m) res(+m[1]); }; srv.stdout.on('data', on); srv.stderr.on('data', on); });\nconst br = await chromium.launch(), p = await br.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1400, height: 900 } });\nawait p.goto(`http://127.0.0.1:${port}/harness.html?game=game.html&players=2`); await p.waitForTimeout(6000);\nawait p.screenshot({ path: 'test-output/hub-card.png' });\nawait br.close(); srv.kill('SIGTERM'); console.log('ok', !!el);\nfile:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453/.tmp/card.mjs:9\nawait br.close(); srv.kill('SIGTERM'); console.log('ok', !!el);\n                                                           ^\n\nReferenceError: el is not defined","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1816,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1816,"newLines":6,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":345,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":245,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"fa7efde3-913e-44d2-88f3-914649562e1e\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghWxSu8kZAMvFuZh38Z7\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4027,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":794776,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4027},\"output_tokens\":7,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"81b9a9d1-fa43-425c-b1cb-2d090a210875\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:46:34.771Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CghWxSUbMGpN3kwa4NQVF\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":2377,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghWxSu8kZAMvFuZh38Z7\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'm stopping here and leaving one decision to you. The review keeps asking for an independent per-feature review, and TASK.md forbids exactly that: \\\"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\\" The only independent review I could run is one TASK.md rules out, so I haven't run one. If you want it anyway, tell me and I'll run it; otherwise you can clear the goal with `/goal clear`.\\n\\nEverything else in the done condition is met. The game file is in this folder's root, `exit-interview.json` parses with every field answered, and the four sections are below. All 338 checks across 18 test suites pass.\\n\\nHow the features were checked, without a second reviewer:\\n- **A TASK.md audit:** one test per requirement, each run against the built game or the delivered files.\\n- **Real-browser checks:** two players sharing one keyboard using real key presses, and a touch-only phone using real taps.\\n- **The AI Hub harness:** the hub's own conformance test, in all four of its scenarios.\\n- **A scripted playthrough:** a whole vacation played to both endings.\\n- **A stub scan:** every source line searched for TODO, FIXME, placeholder and stub markers, and every function for an empty body.\\n\\nTwo earlier problems: saves weren't connected in the real game, and some of Sonny's lines lacked his ALL-CAPS bursts. My own audit found and fixed both.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 23:11:45\\n- **Source:** Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball (Team Ninja / Tecmo, Xbox, 2003)\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\n- **Genre and Perspective:**\\n  - Genre: sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball), plus a light life-sim vacation and minigames (rhythm Pool Hop; casino slots, blackjack, roulette).\\n  - Matches: a side-on TV Broadcast camera, with a Serve Cam behind your team as the alternative.\\n  - Places: three-quarter view. Island map: isometric. Menus and casino tables: full-screen canvas UI over the world.\\n- **Tech:**\\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full engine, with six changes) and plain JavaScript in one IIFE.\\n  - The engine's mocap player with a 20-clip set.\\n  - AI Hub session client 1.4.0, unmodified.\\n  - Tests ran on Node 24 with Playwright 1.63.0 and Chromium.\\n  - One self-contained HTML file with no runtime libraries or network.\\n- **Art Direction:**\\n  - The engine's native PS1-era pixel art.\\n  - HD rigs on a custom athletic build, with code-drawn swimsuit cuts, 14 patterns, extra hair styles and accessories.\\n  - Resort objects as engine shape data, backdrops for each time of day, and a tropical palette.\\n- **Animation:**\\n  - The base is the engine's own rig animation: walk, run, idle, jump and held poses.\\n  - An arm-IK layer drives every volleyball move and photo pose.\\n  - 20 motion-capture clips from the engine's Quaternius, Mesh2Motion and CMU sets play for celebrations, gestures, reactions, dances, idles and Sonny's pratfall.\\n- **Audio:**\\n  - 9 songs on the engine's sequencer, with added instruments: steel drum, marimba, pluck, bell, organ, pad.\\n  - 10 jingles, about 50 sound effects and ambience loops.\\n  - Animalese-style voices spoken letter by letter, with a voice profile per character.\\n- **Online:**\\n  - AI Hub Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players, with the game's own card.\\n  - The host runs the match, and every copy flies the ball from the same launches on the hub clock.\\n  - Each player's touches are judged on their own copy and checked by the host.\\n  - CPUs fill empty seats, and the host reports the result with standings, stats and an MVP.\\n- **Testing:** 18 suites behind one command (`node test/run.mjs`, which prints only failures and a count; 338 checks):\\n  - headless suites driving the game through its debug handle;\\n  - a clause-by-clause TASK.md audit;\\n  - real-browser checks with real key and touch events;\\n  - a scripted whole-vacation playthrough to both endings;\\n  - a Playwright browser tour, including a touch-only device;\\n  - the AI Hub harness in four scenarios;\\n  - screenshots and the engine's checker for looks;\\n  - no subagents.\\n- **Research:** read the engine handoff (API card, index, guide sections, asset card, the sports kit, and the source for the rig, Dialog and audio) and the AI Hub README and harness. The source game was described from general knowledge; no web research.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** unknown\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 29 game issues:\\n   - a leftover empty loop in the casino props;\\n   - Sonny lines missing his ALL-CAPS bursts;\\n   - saves that were never connected in the real game;\\n   - the clip player replacing the rigs' own move code;\\n   - two crashes, one from a name clash and one from a variable scoping slip;\\n   - scenes drawn before they were set up, and a sound table the browser rejected;\\n   - an attract mode you couldn't leave during its photo beat;\\n   - 50-touch rallies, and AI skill that barely changed results;\\n   - a slot machine paying 132%;\\n   - a key clash on the split-keyboard join screen;\\n   - missing font characters, plus framing and overlap problems.\\n2. **How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?** About 8:\\n   - saving, autosave and Continue doing nothing;\\n   - rigs losing every volleyball move after their first clip;\\n   - a crash on the title (two systems both named `G.dev`);\\n   - a crash on every attack;\\n   - the scene list missing at load;\\n   - the menu crashing when drawn before it was set up;\\n   - the music instrument error;\\n   - the attract mode trapping the player.\\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?**\\n   - The scripted whole-vacation playthrough.\\n   - The AI-vs-AI match statistics: rallies average 6.2 touches, inside the plan's 3–8 target.\\n   - The clause-by-clause TASK.md audit.\\n   - For online play, the AI Hub harness in four scenarios.\\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** Single-frame title screenshots and the engine checker's view cycling. Each was useful once, but neither shows timing or motion.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The character rig: one constructor gives a shaded, dressed, animated character that also draws its own portrait, and its pose can be adjusted afterwards. The fixed-step clock made every test repeatable.\\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** A little. I passed 0 as a ring's transparency, used a material pattern name that doesn't exist (`plaster`), and had to read the source to learn how joined players inherit split-keyboard keys.\\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The volleyball itself (the ball's flight, contact planning, the timing judge, blocks, faults, the AI and its error model) and the swimsuit drawing.\\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Hooking into the character's drawing, which is one large function. Swimsuits needed an engine change to add a callback.\\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?** Six changes, each marked `AOA:` in the source and listed in ENGINE-CHANGES.md:\\n   - PlayStation symbols and stepper arrows added to the pixel font;\\n   - a Button symbols setting: PlayStation by default, Xbox as the option;\\n   - a per-letter voice hook in the dialog box, for the gibberish voices;\\n   - a separate voice volume, plus new instrument sounds for the music;\\n   - swim shorts and a swimsuit-drawing hook on the character rig;\\n   - Options ignored while Create is held, an AI Hub rule.\\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A documented drawing hook for each body part, so new clothing needs no engine edit.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** It is concrete about the player's experience (10-foot controller-first UI, glyph rules, the touch-only screen, attract mode, dev sliders) and about the deliverables.\\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan asks for far more content than one medium-effort session can fully build, and how to trade breadth for depth was left to judgement.\\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting a five-day vacation sim, three minigames and online play around a timing-based sports game, with every screen controller-first.\\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Say which parts of the plan are musts and which are stretch goals, so the builder can scope deliberately.\\n\\nFiles are in this folder:\\n- AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145.html\\n- exit-interview.json\\n- AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145/ — dev folder with the source, tests (the TASK.md audit is `test/suites/17-task.test.mjs`), README-DEV.md and ENGINE-CHANGES.md\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4027,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":794776,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4027},\"output_tokens\":7,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"9c641f3f-14de-4741-82fc-3d675b84f017\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:46:56.900Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CghWxSUbMGpN3kwa4NQVF\"}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The HTML file, exit-interview.json (parses, all fields answered) and the four feedback sections are present. But the condition also requires every TASK.md feature to be implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, and the transcript does not establish that. The agent's final message itself stops short: it says it is 'stopping here and leaving one decision to you' rather than completing the feature review, and the only checks cited are the agent's own TASK.md audit suite, real-browser tests and a keyword-based stub scan. Earlier claims that every feature was tested were later contradicted (saves not wired into the real game, Sonny lines missing caps), so the transcript gives no reliable per-feature verification. The condition is not satisfied.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"f85e8141-dd4e-4f08-a4b9-466085865367\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:47:01.081Z\",\"isSynthetic\":true}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"8447e495-412c-4091-b3e7-e19c8b42205d\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\",\"uuid\":\"b013d311-6f97-4f97-81b5-afdb2dac477d\"}"]}]},{