e | tail -1 && timeout 900 node tests/run.mjs --browser 2>&1 | tail -6\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Route cutscene applies through the helper and retest\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":920000}},\\\"wire_ingest_context\\\":{\\\"toolu_01V98nDYyKaZEkLFjF49x1Sh\\\":{\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-215521__x5b1962/work/DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-215521\\\"}}}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"task_started\\\",\\\"task_id\\\":\\\"b6f9q1xm9\\\",\\\"run_id\\\":\\\"0mw1tc17f-6989b769\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01V98nDYyKaZEkLFjF49x1Sh\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"Route cutscene applies through the helper and retest\\\",\\\"is_backgrounded\\\":false,\\\"task_type\\\":\\\"local_bash\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"c6a60761-e0a7-428a-96f2-19d7206ed776\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"9acc64b9-af41-4198-9bbd-536ec13fbed1\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_progress\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01V98nDYyKaZEkLFjF49x1Sh-heartbeat-0\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01V98nDYyKaZEkLFjF49x1Sh\\\",\\\"elapsed_time_seconds\\\":30,\\\"heartbeat\\\":true,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"9acc64b9-af41-4198-9bbd-536ec13fbed1\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"1da3497e-d9e7-4716-b42d-0edbec1f1063\\\"}\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/agent.out\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":2346,\"oldLines\":3,\"newStart\":2346,\"newLines\":5,\"lines\":[\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"task_notification\\\",\\\"task_id\\\":\\\"ba0fcy6ll\\\",\\\"run_id\\\":\\\"0mw1tc9ym-4c5d03d8\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01PA9sStcFJjGv6LR7u9LmnM\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"output_file\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Rerun the hub card screenshot showing errors\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"d42281b0-895d-4d9d-aee5-4e75f4aa1f9d\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"e8aedb0d-fc32-4598-b2c3-8a34e0c85184\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01PA9sStcFJjGv6LR7u9LmnM\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"node:internal/modules/run_main:107\\\\n    triggerUncaughtException(\\\\n    ^\\\\n\\\\nframe.frameElement: Frame has been detached.\\\\n  log: [],\\\\n  name: 'Error'\\\\n}\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"e8aedb0d-fc32-4598-b2c3-8a34e0c85184\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"8fe07780-ef7b-4c09-a070-c5bd6116affe\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T07:46:37.452Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"node:internal/modules/run_main:107\\\\n    triggerUncaughtException(\\\\n    ^\\\\n\\\\nframe.frameElement: Frame has been detached.\\\\n  log: [],\\\\n  name: 'Error'\\\\n}\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false,\\\"bashEditDiff\\\":{\\\"files\\\":[{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/agent.out\\\",\\\"hunks\\\":[{\\\"oldStart\\\":1811,\\\"oldLines\\\":3,\\\"newStart\\\":1811,\\\"newLines\\\":7,\\\"lines\\\":[\\\" {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"msg_011CghWv4L2mx281shoCjk4x\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"thinking\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"thinking\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"signature\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"container\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"stop_reason\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"stop_sequence\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"stop_details\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"usage\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"input_tokens\\\\\\\":2,\\\\\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\\\\\":883,\\\\\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\\\\\":793893,\\\\\\\"cache_creation\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\\\\\":883},\\\\\\\"output_tokens\\\\\\\":8,\\\\\\\"service_tier\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"standard\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"inference_geo\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"global\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"speed\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"standard\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"input_transformations\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"diagnostics\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"context_management\\\\\\\":null},\\\\\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"session_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"uuid\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"59b6e127-9932-462d-b543-5f41a25af95f\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"timestamp\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-11-04T07:46:06.172Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"request_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"req_011CghWv3uyZqxaXhFybNjzE\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"thinking_duration_ms\\\\\\\":6586,\\\\\\\"thinking_display\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"updates\\\\\\\"}\\\",\\\" {\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"msg_011CghWv4L2mx281shoCjk4x\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"role\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assistant\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"content\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"I've deepened the checks the review called shallow, running them in real Chromium with real key and touch events. All 338 checks across 18 suites pass, including the clause-by-clause TASK.md audit, which also confirms the About page and the regenerated exit interview match. The game file is rebuilt.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**What the real-browser checks cover**\\\\\\\\n- **Two players on one keyboard:**\\\\\\\\n  - pressing `2` on the keyboard joins P2;\\\\\\\\n  - pressing F and `.` readies both players and the match starts;\\\\\\\\n  - holding S steers only P1, and the down arrow only P2;\\\\\\\\n  - during play, each player's own hit key (F, or `.`) plays her touches.\\\\\\\\n- **A touch-only phone:**\\\\\\\\n  - a tap on the title doesn't start play;\\\\\\\\n  - no touch buttons or stick appear;\\\\\\\\n  - the attract mode starts after 10 s idle, and a tap ends it.\\\\\\\\n- **Stubs:** every source line is checked for TODO/FIXME/placeholder/stub markers, and every function for an empty body. The empty-function check found one real leftover, an empty loop in the casino props, which I removed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**An independent review isn't possible here.** TASK.md says \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", so the review is my own work plus the tests. The audit suite checks every TASK.md clause against the built game, and the real-browser suite repeats the input-dependent ones with real events.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n**Neither the island map nor rally length is a gap.** The map has every landmark the plan names. Rally length was measured at 6.2 touches on average (median 5), inside the plan's 3–8 target, and the match test enforces that range.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Source Information\\\\\\\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 23:11:45\\\\\\\\n- **Source:** Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball (Team Ninja / Tecmo, Xbox, 2003)\\\\\\\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\\\\\\\n- **Genre and Perspective:**\\\\\\\\n  - Genre: sports (arcade 2v2 beach volleyball), plus a light life-sim vacation (calendar, friendships, gifts, swimsuit collecting) and minigames (rhythm Pool Hop; casino slots, blackjack, roulette).\\\\\\\\n  - Matches: a side-on TV Broadcast camera, with a Serve Cam behind your team as the alternative.\\\\\\\\n  - Places: three-quarter view. Island map: isometric. Shops, casino tables and menus: full-screen canvas UI over the world.\\\\\\\\n- **Tech:**\\\\\\\\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full engine, with six changes) and plain JavaScript in one IIFE.\\\\\\\\n  - The engine's mocap player with a 20-clip set.\\\\\\\\n  - AI Hub session client 1.4.0, unmodified.\\\\\\\\n  - Tests ran on Node 24 with Playwright 1.63.0 and Chromium.\\\\\\\\n  - One self-contained HTML file with no runtime libraries or network.\\\\\\\\n- **Art Direction:**\\\\\\\\n  - The engine's native PS1-era pixel art.\\\\\\\\n  - HD rigs on a custom athletic build, with code-drawn swimsuit cuts, 14 patterns, extra hair styles and accessories.\\\\\\\\n  - Resort objects as engine shape data, backdrops for each time of day, and a tropical palette.\\\\\\\\n- **Animation:**\\\\\\\\n  - The base is the engine's own rig animation: walk, run, idle, jump and held poses.\\\\\\\\n  - An arm-IK layer drives every volleyball move and photo pose, timed from the match's contact plan.\\\\\\\\n  - 20 motion-capture clips, cut from the engine's Quaternius, Mesh2Motion and CMU sets with its `anim-set` tool, play for celebrations, gestures, gift reactions, party dances, idles and Sonny's pratfall.\\\\\\\\n- **Audio:**\\\\\\\\n  - 9 songs on the engine's sequencer, with added instruments: steel drum, marimba, pluck, bell, organ, pad.\\\\\\\\n  - 10 jingles, about 50 sound effects and ambience loops.\\\\\\\\n  - Animalese-style voices spoken letter by letter, with a voice profile per character.\\\\\\\\n- **Online:**\\\\\\\\n  - AI Hub Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players, with the game's own card.\\\\\\\\n  - The host runs the match; every copy flies the ball from the same launches on the hub clock.\\\\\\\\n  - Each player's touches are judged on their own copy and checked by the host.\\\\\\\\n  - CPUs fill empty seats, and the host reports the result with standings, stats and an MVP.\\\\\\\\n- **Testing:** 18 suites behind one command (`node test/run.mjs`, which prints only failures and a count; 338 checks):\\\\\\\\n  - headless suites driving the game through its debug handle (core, data, ball, rules, match, vacation, casino, Pool Hop, UI, attract, dev mode, postcards, motion clips);\\\\\\\\n  - a clause-by-clause TASK.md audit;\\\\\\\\n  - real-browser checks with real key and touch events (two players on one keyboard, a touch-only phone);\\\\\\\\n  - a scripted whole-vacation playthrough to both endings;\\\\\\\\n  - a Playwright browser tour, including a touch-only device;\\\\\\\\n  - the AI Hub harness in four scenarios;\\\\\\\\n  - screenshots and the engine's checker for looks;\\\\\\\\n  - no subagents.\\\\\\\\n- **Research:** read the engine handoff (API card, index, guide sections, asset card, the sports kit, and the source for the rig, Dialog and audio) and the AI Hub README and harness. The source game was described from general knowledge; no web research.\\\\\\\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\\\\\\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\\\\\\\n- **Usage:** unknown\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Testing Feedback\\\\\\\\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 29 game issues:\\\\\\\\n   - a leftover empty loop in the casino props;\\\\\\\\n   - Sonny lines missing his ALL-CAPS bursts;\\\\\\\\n   - saves that were never connected in the real game (only the tests set them up);\\\\\\\\n   - the clip player replacing the rigs' own move code;\\\\\\\\n   - two crashes, one from a name clash and one from a variable scoping slip;\\\\\\\\n   - scenes drawn before they were set up, and a sound table the browser rejected;\\\\\\\\n   - an attract mode you couldn't leave during its photo beat;\\\\\\\\n   - 50-touch rallies, and AI skill that barely changed results;\\\\\\\\n   - a slot machine paying 132%;\\\\\\\\n   - a key clash on the split-keyboard join screen;\\\\\\\\n   - missing font characters, plus framing and overlap problems on several screens.\\\\\\\\n2. **How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?** About 8:\\\\\\\\n   - saving, autosave and Continue doing nothing;\\\\\\\\n   - rigs losing every volleyball move after their first clip;\\\\\\\\n   - a crash on the title (two systems both named `G.dev`);\\\\\\\\n   - a crash on every attack;\\\\\\\\n   - the scene list missing at load;\\\\\\\\n   - the menu crashing when drawn before it was set up;\\\\\\\\n   - the music instrument error;\\\\\\\\n   - the attract mode trapping the player.\\\\\\\\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?**\\\\\\\\n   - The scripted whole-vacation playthrough (both endings, every story event, casino, Pool Hop, saves).\\\\\\\\n   - The AI-vs-AI match statistics: rallies average 6.2 touches, inside the 3–8 target.\\\\\\\\n   - The clause-by-clause TASK.md audit.\\\\\\\\n   - For online play, the AI Hub harness in four scenarios.\\\\\\\\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** Single-frame title screenshots and the engine checker's view cycling. Each was useful once, but neither shows timing or motion, which only the scripted runs caught.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Engine Feedback\\\\\\\\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The character rig. One constructor gives a shaded, dressed, animated character that also draws its own portrait, and its pose can be adjusted afterwards. So swimsuits, new hair and every volleyball move were additions, not rewrites. The fixed-step clock made every test repeatable.\\\\\\\\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** A little. I passed 0 as a ring's transparency, used a material pattern name that doesn't exist (`plaster`), and had to read the source to learn how joined players inherit split-keyboard keys. The index answered most other questions.\\\\\\\\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The volleyball itself: the ball's flight, contact planning, the timing judge, blocks, faults, and the AI and its error model. Also the swimsuit cuts and patterns drawn on the torso.\\\\\\\\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Hooking into the character's drawing, which is one large function. Swimsuits needed an engine change to add a callback.\\\\\\\\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?** Six changes, each marked `AOA:` in the source and listed in ENGINE-CHANGES.md:\\\\\\\\n   - PlayStation symbols and stepper arrows added to the pixel font;\\\\\\\\n   - a Button symbols setting: PlayStation by default, Xbox as the option, in the Game group;\\\\\\\\n   - a per-letter voice hook in the dialog box, for the gibberish voices;\\\\\\\\n   - a separate voice volume, plus new instrument sounds for the music (named waves, pluck decay, lowpass, detune);\\\\\\\\n   - swim shorts and a swimsuit-drawing hook on the character rig;\\\\\\\\n   - Options ignored while Create is held, an AI Hub rule.\\\\\\\\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A documented drawing hook for each body part, so new clothing needs no engine edit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## Prompt Feedback\\\\\\\\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** It is concrete about the player's experience (10-foot controller-first UI, glyph rules, the touch-only screen, attract mode, dev sliders) and about the deliverables, so it's clear when the work is done.\\\\\\\\n2. **What was confusing?** The plan asks for far more content than one medium-effort session can fully build, and how to trade breadth for depth was left to judgement.\\\\\\\\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting a five-day vacation sim, three minigames and online play around a timing-based sports game, with every screen controller-first.\\\\\\\\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Say which parts of the plan are musts and which are stretch goals, so the builder can scope deliberately.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFiles are in this folder:\\\\\\\\n- AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145.html\\\\\\\\n- exit-interview.json\\\\\\\\n- AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145/ — dev folder with the source, tests (the TASK.md audit is `test/suites/17-task.test.mjs`, the real-browser checks `test/suites/18-real.test.mjs`), README-DEV.md and ENGINE-CHANGES.md\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"container\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"stop_reason\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"stop_sequence\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"stop_details\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"usage\\\\\