racks take `decay`, `filter` + `cutoff`, `detune` and an instrument as `wave` | a tropical score (steel drum, marimba, plucks, pads) and voices with their own level | data (songs build), browser |\n| 5 | `Humanoid`: an `athletic` build; `outfit: 'swim'` with 7 cuts (one-piece, racer, halter, sport two-piece, tankini, rash guard, sarong) and 14 patterns filled pixel by pixel; `o.pattern` on shirts; `o.shorts`; hair `twinbuns`, `bun`, `braid`, `bob`, `puff`, `curly`; hats `sunhat`, `visor`; an `extras` hook (accessories drawn at head, face, neck, hair and wrist anchors, depth sorted); sandal straps (`colors.strap`) over bare feet; 14 held poses (vready, bump, set, toss, highfive, clap, facepalm, peace, lookback, stretch, sit, sunbathe, spikearm, blockup); explicit pose weights (`state.poseW`) and a timed arm and body overlay (`rig.arms`: hand targets, crouch, lean, twist) | the cast in swimsuits and accessories, and volleyball moves timed to the simulation | rig sheets (`tools/rigsheet.mjs cast|suits|poses|acc|clips`), every suite draws them in the browser |\n| 6 | `input.reserveCombo = [8, 9]`: while Create is held, Options presses reach no action | the AI Hub's corner bar (Create + Options) | hub harness |\n| 7 | `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })`: no touch buttons or stick, no Touch settings group, the corner's menu kept | touch-only devices get a notice instead of touch controls | ui, browser (an emulated phone) |\n| 8 | `E.onStep(fn)`: a hook on every step's input pass, through fades and pauses | the attract must end on any input, even during a scene transition | attract |\n\nGame code also registers two views, `court` (Broadcast: yaw 12, pitch 30, scale 1.5) and `servecam` (yaw -90, pitch 46), in `E.VIEWS`.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VhxETiPYqhSSwhjeDyEyZU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghX4LsAKLCC88bPCjcgQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nwm8iE6PLXkgPr9toQU5Pr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453/README-DEV.md","content":"# Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball (developer notes)\n\n## Build, run, test\n\n```sh\nnpm install                      # Playwright 1.63.0, for the browser tests and tools\nnode tools/build.mjs             # build/game.js, build/dev.html and the deliverable ../<name>.html\nnode test/run.mjs                # every suite: prints only failures and one count line (exit 1 on a failure)\nnode test/run.mjs --only=match,ai --skip-browser --skip-hub\nnode tools/tour.mjs [regex]      # screenshots of every screen into test-output/tour/\nnode tools/rigsheet.mjs cast|suits|poses|acc|clips [fighter]   # rig sheets into test-output/rigsheet/\n```\n\nOpen `build/dev.html` (separate scripts) or the deliverable straight from `file://`.\n\n## Layout\n\n- `src/*.js`: game modules, concatenated in name order into one IIFE (`const E = My3D2dge, G = {}`; `window.AOA = G`).\n  00 core, 01 tuning (every dev slider), 02-06 data (cast, items, world, text, music), 10 input, 11 UI kit, 12 audio,\n  13 rigs, 14 world art, 15 animation, 20-26 volleyball (ball, rules, players, AI, match, netplay, match scene),\n  30-34 vacation (state, map, places, shops, story), 40 Pool Hop, 41 casino, 42 postcards, 50 title, 51 attract,\n  52 Beach Match, 53 dev mode, 54 results, 55 About, 99 main.\n- `engine/my-3d2dge.js`: the patched engine (see `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`); `vendor/`: the AI Hub client (unmodified) and the\n  mocap player with the cut clip set `AOA` (31 clips); `hub/`: the harness (tests only); `.src/`: the engine repository.\n- `test/`: `run.mjs`, `lib/` (the headless loader, bots, the fake hub), `suites/` (19 suites).\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Gameplay never calls `Math.random`: `G.rng('world' | 'match' | 'casino' | 'cosmetic' | ...)` (a test greps for it).\n- Every system reads `G.T` each step (the dev panel's live sliders).\n- Scenes are single objects reused on every visit: reset their state in `enter`.\n- `game.debug.tools` drives everything the dev panel does; tests use the same calls.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3561,"cache_read_input_tokens":924358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3561},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8aedb0d-fc32-4598-b2c3-8a34e0c85184","uuid":"5630218d-ce0e-4f52-b4a1-103cee8b7c6d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:48:12.130Z","request_id":"req_011CghX4LTbkJCenSKF4SaN8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Nwm8iE6PLXkgPr9toQU5Pr":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453/README-DEV.md","content":"# Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball (developer notes)\n\n## Build, run, test\n\n```sh\nnpm install                      # Playwright 1.63.0, for the browser tests and tools\nnode tools/build.mjs             # build/game.js, build/dev.html and the deliverable ../<name>.html\nnode test/run.mjs                # every suite: prints only failures and one count line (exit 1 on a failure)\nnode test/run.mjs --only=match,ai --skip-browser --skip-hub\nnode tools/tour.mjs [regex]      # screenshots of every screen into test-output/tour/\nnode tools/rigsheet.mjs cast|suits|poses|acc|clips [fighter]   # rig sheets into test-output/rigsheet/\n```\n\nOpen `build/dev.html` (separate scripts) or the deliverable straight from `file://`.\n\n## Layout\n\n- `src/*.js`: game modules, concatenated in name order into one IIFE (`const E = My3D2dge, G = {}`; `window.AOA = G`).\n  00 core, 01 tuning (every dev slider), 02-06 data (cast, items, world, text, music), 10 input, 11 UI kit, 12 audio,\n  13 rigs, 14 world art, 15 animation, 20-26 volleyball (ball, rules, players, AI, match, netplay, match scene),\n  30-34 vacation (state, map, places, shops, story), 40 Pool Hop, 41 casino, 42 postcards, 50 title, 51 attract,\n  52 Beach Match, 53 dev mode, 54 results, 55 About, 99 main.\n- `engine/my-3d2dge.js`: the patched engine (see `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`); `vendor/`: the AI Hub client (unmodified) and the\n  mocap player with the cut clip set `AOA` (31 clips); `hub/`: the harness (tests only); `.src/`: the engine repository.\n- `test/`: `run.mjs`, `lib/` (the headless loader, bots, the fake hub), `suites/` (19 suites).\n\n## Conventions\n\n- Gameplay never calls `Math.random`: `G.rng('world' | 'match' | 'casino' | 'cosmetic' | ...)` (a test greps for it).\n- Every system reads `G.T` each step (the dev panel's live sliders).\n- Scenes are single objects reused on every visit: reset their state in `enter`.\n- `game.debug.tools` drives everything the dev panel does; tests use the same calls.\n"}}}
