{"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","uuid":"391a9beb-16cb-43b2-9bf6-62f679082fc7","compact_metadata":{"trigger":"auto","pre_tokens":972239,"post_tokens":16819,"cumulative_dropped_tokens":955420,"duration_ms":73444,"preserved_segment":{"head_uuid":"d09cc0e1-99cb-4a93-acda-8b35814aa5a7","anchor_uuid":"0d316c2e-d770-42ac-98e0-97d0257172be","tail_uuid":"afa04f8e-b522-4f80-b554-1460e46fb07c"},"preserved_messages":{"anchor_uuid":"0d316c2e-d770-42ac-98e0-97d0257172be","uuids":["d09cc0e1-99cb-4a93-acda-8b35814aa5a7","60cddba7-a465-49a4-8b0d-7dd9ca7e5510","6fcbd45b-d625-47ad-b4e6-0c1985b02a6d","afa04f8e-b522-4f80-b554-1460e46fb07c"],"all_uuids":["d09cc0e1-99cb-4a93-acda-8b35814aa5a7","60cddba7-a465-49a4-8b0d-7dd9ca7e5510","6fcbd45b-d625-47ad-b4e6-0c1985b02a6d","afa04f8e-b522-4f80-b554-1460e46fb07c"]}},"logical_parent_uuid":"afa04f8e-b522-4f80-b554-1460e46fb07c","session_id":"e8aedb0d-fc32-4598-b2c3-8a34e0c85184"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n\n   STAGE.md says to build the game in TASK.md following PLAN.md, using its title; where they disagree, TASK.md wins. The title is \"Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball\", a riff on Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball. Names and date come from TASK.md:\n   - Dev folder: `AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453/`\n   - Deliverable: `...-20261103-225453.html` in the work root.\n   - Date: 2026-11-03 22:54:53.\n\n   TASK.md requires all of the following:\n   - A feature-complete demo on the my-3d2dge engine.\n   - Dev mode from the pause menu, with tools and live sliders and a reset to defaults.\n   - An attract mode after 10 s idle on the title or menu; any input exits it.\n   - AI Hub multiplayer per lib/hub, plus local play.\n   - A 10-foot, controller-first UI: PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option; native keyboard and mouse with hover focus; prompts that follow the last device.\n   - Touch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button; the attract still runs.\n   - All audio in code, with gibberish voices.\n   - An About/Credits screen and the final reply, both with Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback (\"unknown\" for anything unconfirmable).\n   - exit-interview.json in an exact shape.\n\n   Constraints from TASK.md, verbatim:\n   - \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"\n   - \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check. Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"\n   - Do not commit or push unless asked. Do not send the user's email anywhere.\n\n   The Stop hook then rejected completion. It said the figures were unmeasured (\"about 760 checks\", \"about 30 issues\", \"about 60 sound effects\", \"roughly two hours\"). It also said these were unverified end to end:\n   - the attract playlist montage beats (as captured in screenshots);\n   - the Serve Cam view in a live match;\n   - the 4-player Beach Match on pads;\n   - the PlayStation glyphs with a pad;\n   - the \"Clean\" mode;\n   - the scene-state-persisting bug class.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - The my-3D2dge v0.85.2 engine (handoff copy, patched):\n     - Scenes, `game.go` (a fade delays the switch), `game.advance` fixed 1/120 s steps, headless in Node, `game.debug`.\n     - E.Humanoid rigs, E.Dialog, E.Shell, E.TileMap, r.shape, E.SHAPES / E.MATERIALS, lights, audio music clock.\n     - Input presets: `input.use`, halfKeys, allowJoin / addPlayer.\n   - The closed-form ball flight (drag k, gravity g, wind ay, wobble). Each launch precomputes tNet / netAt / tLand / landIn.\n   - Contact planning: who plays the ball, t*, P*, contact height. Then the timing judge (PERFECT / GREAT / OK / MISS windows × assist), AI quality rolls with pressure and hard-ball penalties, and spectacle mode.\n   - Random streams through `G.rng(name)` (world / match / casino / cosmetic); gameplay never calls Math.random.\n   - The AI Hub shared world:\n     - host-authoritative; clients judge their own touches and send claims ('c', 'v');\n     - snapshots 's', launches 'b', events 'e';\n     - our own card; finish() with standings.\n   - Mocap clips: the cut AOA set (31 clips) played through `Mocap.drive`. `Mocap` and `MOCAP` are top-level script names, not window properties.\n   - Scene objects are reused on every visit, so their state must be reset in `enter`.\n   - Testing: test/run.mjs plus suites; Playwright 1.63.0 Chromium; a fake hub in Node; the AI Hub harness served on 127.0.0.1.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all relative to the DEV folder unless noted):\n   - **engine/my-3d2dge.js**: the patched engine; patches are marked `// AOA:`.\n     1. Font glyphs: ✕○□△◀▶▼✓♠♦♣ ·…—’² ¡íéèóáñú.\n     2. `glyphs` setting in the Game group: playstation default, xbox option.\n     3. Dialog: a function voice called per letter; `say()` takes voice and nameColor.\n     4. Audio: `_voxBus`, a `voices` setting, `audio.bus()`, `audio.instruments` / `_inst` PeriodicWave, decay/filter/cutoff/detune on tracks.\n     5. Humanoid (tools/patches/p5-humanoid.py, p5b-draw.py, p5c-shorts.py):\n        - athletic build; swim outfit with swimRegion and aoaFillTorso per-pixel patterns (SWIM_PATTERNS); patterned shirt; o.shorts;\n        - hair twinbuns/bun/braid/bob/puff/curly (aoaHairShapes); hats sunhat/visor;\n        - the extras hook; colors.strap;\n        - AOA_POSES and aoaHands; `s.poseW` explicit weights; `rig.arms` overlay.\n     6. input.reserveCombo (Create + Options).\n     7. `touch: 'never'` → input.noTouch, now set right after Input creation.\n     8. `E.onStep(fn)`, which pushes to HOOKS.input so it runs every step, through fades and pauses.\n   - **src/** has 35 files. Notable ones:\n     - 00-core: G namespace, streams, bus, overlay; wrapScene removes `sceneBound` overlays on enter; G.scenes = {}.\n     - 01-tuning: 37 sliders.\n     - Data files: 02-data-cast, 03-data-items, 04-data-world (G.LOCS, G.ISLAND), 05-data-text (345 lines), 06-data-music (9 songs from a song builder, 10 jingles).\n     - 10-input: presets MATCH / EXPLORE / MENU / POOLHOP / CASINO; G.dev(I) for glyph style; G.glyph / G.prompt / G.promptBar; G.pushInput / G.popInput; G.touchOnly.\n     - 11-ui: G.Nav, widgets, icons, G.confirm, toasts, `G.tenFootCSS()` (scales the Shell's HTML text).\n     - 12-audio: 50 SFX, G.voice Animalese, ambience.\n     - 13-rigs: G.makeRig, accessories.\n     - 14-world-art: TOD presets, G.paintSky, court map, shapes, crowd, props, net, fx.\n     - 15-anim: G.Anim.player / idle / clip.\n     - Volleyball:\n       - 20-ball: G.Ball.\n       - 21-rules: G.Rules.\n       - 22-players: VB.judge, makePlayer, aimTarget.\n       - 23-ai: AI.roll(M, p, stat, incoming, slack), shotTarget, attackTarget.\n       - 24-match: G.Match. Specials: Golden Glare / dazzled, House Edge (`L.houseEdge` excludes a partner with affinity < 60), Lucky Seven. Also replays, the HUD, a CPU fallback to a shot when a spike can't clear, the held ball shown in the nearer hand.\n       - 25-netplay: G.Net, the hub scene and card.\n       - 26-matchscene: the match scene and G.resultsUI.\n     - Vacation:\n       - 30-vacation: state, dayStart / slotStart / endSlot / dayEnd, gifts, invite, G.setPartner, matchPayout, saves, unlocks. Newly added:\n         ```js\n         G.resumeVacation = () => { const st = G.state; if (!st) return; G.seed('world', st.seed * 31 + st.day * 7 + st.slot); G.game.go('map', null, { fade: 'white', seconds: .4 }); };\n         ```\n       - 31-map: the map resets `finalAsked` on enter.\n       - 32-location: talk / bag / board / letter UI; L.zoom; `this.near = null` reset on enter.\n       - 33-shop: shop, wardrobe, journal.\n       - 34-story: invitation, charselect, cutscene engine (enter now resets `finished, skipTutorial, ff, fwT, flam, wheel`), CUTSCENES arrival / tutorialDone / party / endingA / endingB, startVacationMatch, afterVacationMatch, story hooks.\n     - Minigames and extras:\n       - 40-poolhop: the beat is relative to entry (b0); enter resets base / baseI / botDone / bonus / cheerT / judge; `auto` (dev autopilot, records results) differs from `bot` (attract demo bot).\n       - 41-casino: Slots with blank stops, RTP about 92%; BJ, ROULETTE.\n       - 42-photo: photo mode overlay (sceneBound, pushInput('MENU')), specs, album, renderSpec.\n       - 50-title: title, menu, howto / about pages, G.touchGate, howtoOverlay.\n       - 51-attract: BEATS, director, E.onStep input watcher.\n       - 52-exhibition: Beach Match 1–4 players.\n       - 53-dev: G.devPanel (renamed from G.dev), G.debugTools, G.debugHandle.\n       - 54-results: dayend, credits (done reset), vresults.\n       - 55-about: G.ABOUT with credits / source / testing / engine / prompt arrays. Its numbers must now be made exact.\n       - 99-main: Game options, SETTINGS, pause items as a function, Shell theme (font family) plus `G.tenFootCSS()`, boot.\n   - **vendor/**: aihub-session.js (unmodified 1.4.0); mocap/readable.js, mocap.js, aoa-clips.js (31 clips, 219 KB).\n   - **tools/**:\n     - build.mjs (writes build/game.js, build/dev.html and the deliverable with the hub client first after meta charset, plus the hub meta tags);\n     - rigsheet.mjs (modes: cast | suits | poses | acc | clips);\n     - shot.mjs; tour.mjs (STOPS list); sheet.mjs (contact sheets);\n     - interview.mjs (writes ../exit-interview.json from G.ABOUT and validates it);\n     - the handoff's check.mjs and others; patches/.\n   - **test/**:\n     - run.mjs: the ORDER now includes 'saves' and 'revisit' before 'netcode'.\n     - lib/load.mjs: vm loader; options hub, perfNow, touchOnly, noBoot.\n     - lib/bots.mjs: aiMatch, runMatch (stuck = no phase change and no touch for 15 s), startCfg, talkThrough, playUntil, finishMatch(G, game, win, force).\n     - lib/fakehub.mjs.\n     - suites: core, data (includes a glyph-coverage check), ball, rules, judge, ai, match, vacation, shop, story, poolhop, casino, ui, attract, dev, saves (new), revisit (new), netcode, playthrough, browser, hub.\n   - **Docs**:\n     - ENGINE-CHANGES.md: a table of the 8 patches.\n     - README-DEV.md.\n     - ../exit-interview.json: written by tools/interview.mjs; parses; every field filled. It still contains the \"about\" figures and must be regenerated after 55-about.js is updated.\n\n4. Errors and fixes (chronological highlights):\n   - Load order: G.scenes undefined → defined in 00-core.\n   - Slots RTP was 153% → strips with 6 blanks per reel (exactly 92.0%).\n   - Rallies too long or \"stuck\" → AI.roll penalties for hard balls and pressure; fewer cut shots; shotTarget; blocks attempted less often and beaten by stronger spikes; fewer AI serve faults; kills credited when a dig fails.\n   - The perfect bot lost → cpuControl plus PERFECT touches and serves; a CPU attacker that can't clear the net cuts a shot instead.\n   - Critical game bugs:\n     - Ingrid had no tutorial partner → G.setPartner.\n     - The cutscene `finished` flag → reset in enter.\n     - Pool Hop's beat origin → b0.\n     - The map's finalAsked → reset.\n     - The credits' done flag → reset.\n     - The G.dev / G.devPanel name clash crashed the title draw → renamed.\n     - Continue / Load crashed (G.resumeVacation was missing; found by the new revisit test) → defined.\n   - Screenshot findings fixed: the title camera; net edge-on (court view now yaw 12, pitch 30); the crowd's position; Serve Cam yaw -90; missing glyphs; the night-lighting gap; toast position; talk-panel overlap; pool texture; location zoom; shop and casino text layout; dev full-width rows off-screen; overlays lacking menu actions (pushInput); overlays persisting across scenes (sceneBound); intro title overlap; the held ball hidden; tiny Shell text (font family plus tenFootCSS); mocap globals.\n   - Test-side fixes: RK4 integrator; startCfg waits for the scene; cloned configs; held keys in Playwright; polling for the first point; excluding a player who left; RANDOM fields ignored in revisit; key-field comparison in saves.\n   - Stop-hook feedback (the user's side): the claims weren't measured and features weren't verified end to end. Being addressed now.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Done:\n   - Full test run: 762 passed / 0 failed in 19 suites. This was before the saves and revisit suites; those two now pass 34 / 0.\n   - The AI Hub harness passes all 4 scenarios.\n   - The deliverable is built: 2,031 KB; no external loads; no TODO or placeholder text.\n   - The hub card was screenshotted and looks right.\n\n   Measured: SFX 50, songs 9, jingles 10, clips 31, suits 21, accessories 10, gifts 25, sliders 37, dialogue lines 345, src 5742 lines.\n\n   Session time: start 2026-11-03 22:54:53; last check 2026-11-04 00:54:27 (about 2 h). Re-run `date` at the end for the exact span.\n\n   Critical game-breaking bugs found: 7 (the 6 earlier plus the Continue/Load crash).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The `/goal` command, quoted in full in section 1.\n   - Stop hook feedback: \"Not satisfied. The html and exit-interview.json exist and parse, and the final reply has all four sections. But the transcript shows gaps against TASK.md: the About text claims 'about 760 checks' and per-claim figures the transcript never measured (e.g. 'about 30 issues', 'about 60 sound effects', 'roughly two hours'); the final reply's 'Testing Feedback' and 'Engine Feedback' answers are said to be 'about' counts; the game's 'Clean' mode is unverified, and PlayStation glyph behavior with a real pad was never tested (only headless). Those are honesty issues rather than missing features. The stronger issue is 'every feature in TASK.md implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs': the transcript never verified several TASK.md items end to end, including the 10-second attract playlist montage beats as captured in screenshots, the Serve Cam view on a live match, and the 4-player Beach Match on real pads. The test run passing does not establish those, and the transcript shows at least one mid-session bug class (scene state persisting) that tests only caught after the fact. Therefore the feature-completeness condition is not clearly evidenced.\"\n   - (Earlier system reminders asked for brief status updates; they were complied with.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Browser test with emulated gamepads, via a Playwright addInitScript that stubs navigator.getGamepads with standard-mapping pads (DualSense id, 17 buttons, axes):\n     - 4 players in Beach Match: P1 on the keyboard left half, P2 on the right half (key '2'), P3 and P4 on pads 1 and 2 joining with Start (button 9) and readying with button 0;\n     - verify the badges and per-device prompt glyphs (PS ✕ for pads, keycaps for the halves), that each human fighter moves in the match, and that the Xbox setting switches the glyphs to A;\n     - screenshot it. Be honest that pads were emulated, not real hardware.\n   - Attract: in the browser, screenshot each beat (match, map, friends, suits, pool, casino, photo, final, card), make a contact sheet and review it.\n   - Serve Cam during a live rally: screenshot and review; improve framing if needed.\n   - Photo filters (Clean, Sunny, Sepia, Retro, Night Glow): screenshots. The \"Clean\" mode probably refers to the photo filter or the engine's Screen filter Clean.\n   - Write TESTING-LOG.md with the exact enumerated list of issues found: tests vs screenshots, critical ones, and game bugs vs test bugs. Count precisely.\n   - Update src/55-about.js with exact figures: the final test count, 50 sound effects, exact issue counts, 7 critical issues, and session start/end times measured with `date`. Remove the \"about\" wording. Mention that the pads were emulated.\n   - Rerun `node tools/interview.mjs` and validate the JSON.\n   - Run the full `node test/run.mjs` and rebuild with `node tools/build.mjs`.\n   - Stop only my own servers by PID.\n   - Give a final reply with the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections, using exact numbers that match the About text and the exit interview.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I am responding to the Stop-hook rejection. So far I have:\n   - Measured the exact counts (sfx 50, etc.).\n   - Created test/suites/revisit.test.mjs (re-enters 27 scene/data combinations after random input and compares simple own fields; RANDOM = msg, quip, _qs, fwT).\n   - Created test/suites/saves.test.mjs (Continue from the menu goes to the map with the same key fields; a slot save and load; the slot level reads 'Day 3 · Afternoon').\n   - Added both to the ORDER in test/run.mjs.\n   - Fixed the bugs they found: G.resumeVacation in 30-vacation.js; location `this.near = null`; Pool Hop state resets; cutscene field resets.\n   - The last command, `node test/run.mjs --only=revisit,saves`, output: \"34 passed, 0 failed (saves, revisit) in 2 s\".\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue addressing the Stop-hook feedback: \"the 10-second attract playlist montage beats as captured in screenshots, the Serve Cam view on a live match, and the 4-player Beach Match on real pads\" and \"PlayStation glyph behavior with a real pad was never tested (only headless)\".\n   - Next: add an emulated-gamepad 4-player Beach Match and glyph check to the browser suite, plus attract-beat, Serve Cam and photo-filter screenshots, and review them.\n   - Then replace the unmeasured \"about\" figures (per the hook: \"'about 760 checks' ... 'about 30 issues', 'about 60 sound effects', 'roughly two hours'\") with exact measured values in src/55-about.js, TESTING-LOG.md and exit-interview.json (via tools/interview.mjs).\n   - Then rerun the full suite and give the final reply with all four sections.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build--20261103-225453--x8def6b-work/e8aedb0d-fc32-4598-b2c3-8a34e0c85184.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8aedb0d-fc32-4598-b2c3-8a34e0c85184","uuid":"0d316c2e-d770-42ac-98e0-97d0257172be","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:57:41.221Z","isSynthetic":true}
