{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghZ98qz1H4Xm8NnKo3Zu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ui9rbygrnUnHodKUXAfyR8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/55-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:60]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"10 jingles, about 60 sound effects, ambience loops\", \"10 jingles, 50 sound effects, ambience loops\")\nrep(\"\"\"['Testing', 'One command (node test/run.mjs) that prints only failures and a count: 19 suites and about 760 checks. Headless Node runs with game.advance and game.debug: units (ball flight, rules, judge, data), AI-vs-AI match statistics, the vacation, shops, story, minigames, UI, attract, dev mode, a fake-hub netcode test at 150 ms latency, jitter and 5% loss, and a scripted playthrough of the whole vacation as all six fighters to both endings. Playwright from file:// (a tour, the attract, an emulated touch-only phone), the engine\\\\'s tools/check.mjs, the AI Hub harness on 127.0.0.1 (4 scenarios), and screenshots and rig sheets for art.'],\"\"\",\n\"\"\"['Testing', 'One command (node test/run.mjs) that prints only failures and a count: 22 suites and @CHECKS@ checks, all passing on the final run. Headless in Node with game.advance and game.debug: units (ball flight, rules, judge, data), AI-vs-AI match statistics, the vacation, shops, story, minigames, UI, attract, dev mode, saves, revisiting all 27 scene setups after random input, a fake-hub netcode test at 150 ms latency with jitter and 5% loss, and a scripted playthrough of the whole vacation as all six fighters, to both endings. In Chromium via Playwright from file://: a tour, the attract, an emulated touch-only phone, and a four-player Beach Match on two keyboard halves and two emulated controllers (navigator.getGamepads stubbed with standard-mapping pads). That run checks PlayStation and Xbox glyphs, Serve Cam in a live rally, every attract beat and every photo filter. No physical controller was tested. Also the engine\\\\'s tools/check.mjs, the AI Hub harness on 127.0.0.1 (4 scenarios), and screenshots and rig sheets for the art. TESTING-LOG.md lists every issue found.'],\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"['Usage', 'unknown (no cost or token meter was available to the model; the build session ran from about 22:55 on 2026-11-03 to about 01:00 on 2026-11-04, roughly two hours)']\"\"\",\n\"\"\"['Usage', 'Cost and tokens unknown (no meter was available to the model). By the system clock the build ran from 2026-11-03 22:54:53 (TASK.md\\\\'s start time) to @END@ when this text was last updated, @SPAN@.']\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"['How many issues did testing catch?', 'About 30. Scripted tests caught about 20 (rallies that never ended because the AI dug everything, a perfect bot losing because the CPU spiked into the net, a starter partner never assigned, scene state that stuck between visits, Pool Hop\\\\'s beat clock, the attract missing input during fades, a touch flag set only in browsers, a name clash between two modules) and screenshots about 10 (night lighting, overlapping text and panels, tiny text in the engine\\\\'s HTML menus, off-screen dev sliders).'],\"\"\",\n\"\"\"['How many issues did testing catch?', '47 game issues, each listed in TESTING-LOG.md. Scripted tests caught 20, for example: rallies that never ended because the AI dug everything; a perfect player losing because the CPU spiked into the net; a starting partner never assigned; scene state carried from one visit to the next; Continue and Load crashing; Pool Hop\\\\'s beat clock; the attract missing input during fades. Screenshots and rig sheets caught 27, for example: the net seen edge-on; overlapping text and panels; tiny text in the engine\\\\'s HTML menus; two menu actions on one key for keyboard-half players; Serve Cam cutting off a player. Separately, 10 bugs in the tests themselves.'],\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', 'Six: the Welcome Match never starting for Ingrid (no one liked her enough to partner up), the game freezing after the Welcome Match (a cutscene flag left set from the arrival), Pool Hop unwinnable when entered from the pool, the Final never being called on a second vacation, the credits never ending on a second run, and the title crashing while drawing its prompt in the browser (a name clash).'],\"\"\",\n\"\"\"['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', 'Seven: the Welcome Match never starting for Ingrid (no one liked her enough to partner up); the game freezing after the Welcome Match (a cutscene flag left set from the arrival); Pool Hop unwinnable when entered from the pool; the Final never called on a second vacation; the credits never ending on a second run; the title crashing while drawing its prompt in the browser (a name clash); and Continue and Load crashing (a missing function).'],\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"It found most of the critical bugs, all of them state that only breaks on a later step or a second run.'],\"\"\",\n\"\"\"It found 5 of the 7 critical bugs, all of them state that only breaks on a later step or a second run. The revisit test (every scene entered twice, with random input in between) found the 7th.'],\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"And at yaw 0 the Broadcast view saw the net edge-on.'],\"\"\",\n\"\"\"And at yaw 0 the Broadcast view saw the net edge-on. I also trusted Input.halfKeys with menu presets: it gave two menu actions the same key, and I only noticed in a four-player screenshot.'],\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"(8) E.onStep, a hook that runs through fades and pauses, so the attract ends on any input.'],\"\"\",\n\"\"\"(8) E.onStep, a hook that runs through fades and pauses, so the attract ends on any input. (9) Input.halfKeys gives each action a button no earlier action holds, so a menu preset\\\\'s alt and extra no longer share keys with confirm and cancel on a keyboard half.'],\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -c \"@CHECKS@\\|@END@\\|@SPAN@\" src/55-about.js; grep -n \"about [0-9]\\|About [0-9]\\|roughly\\|approximately\" src/55-about.js | head","description":"Replace estimated figures in the About text"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":749,"cache_read_input_tokens":158364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":749},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8aedb0d-fc32-4598-b2c3-8a34e0c85184","uuid":"3a62dc48-7c44-4ac5-b4bc-ef8f5be6acc1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:15:35.414Z","request_id":"req_011CghZ98TuZBgxKfGQYzbUQ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Ui9rbygrnUnHodKUXAfyR8":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/55-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:60]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"10 jingles, about 60 sound effects, ambience loops\", \"10 jingles, 50 sound effects, ambience loops\")\nrep(\"\"\"['Testing', 'One command (node test/run.mjs) that prints only failures and a count: 19 suites and about 760 checks. Headless Node runs with game.advance and game.debug: units (ball flight, rules, judge, data), AI-vs-AI match statistics, the vacation, shops, story, minigames, UI, attract, dev mode, a fake-hub netcode test at 150 ms latency, jitter and 5% loss, and a scripted playthrough o