owser alone, hub alone, and the full run above. They are unexplained, not","+fixed.","+"," ## Controllers"," "," The Beach Match, glyph and Xbox checks in `test/suites/pads.test.mjs` use emulated controllers. Chromium's"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453/src/55-about.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":20,"oldLines":11,"newStart":20,"newLines":11,"lines":["     ['Animation', 'The engine\\'s procedural Humanoid rig, extended with 14 held poses and a timed arm and body overlay driven by the volleyball simulation (a spike\\'s jump starts at its contact time minus its rise), plus 31 motion-capture clips played through Mocap.drive for celebrations, idles, dances, swimming and reactions.'],","     ['Audio', 'All in code with Web Audio: 9 original songs from a chord-aware song builder (steel, marimba, bell, organ and pluck instruments; a rally drum layer; a tempo lift at match point; key changes), 10 jingles, 50 sound effects, ambience loops (waves, wind, crowd, pool, casino, crickets) and Animalese-style gibberish voices synthesized letter by letter for every speaker.'],","     ['Online', 'AI Hub sessions (shared world, 1-4 players): the game\\'s own card, one match on the hub\\'s clock, host-authoritative rules and AI, every copy flying the ball from the same launches, client-judged touches the host validates, snapshots for positions, CPUs for empty or left seats, finish() with standings, awards and stats.'],","-    ['Testing', 'One command (node test/run.mjs) that prints only failures and a count: 22 suites and @CHECKS@ checks, all passing on the final run. Headless in Node with game.advance and game.debug: units (ball flight, rules, judge, data), AI-vs-AI match statistics, the vacation, shops, story, minigames, UI, attract, dev mode, saves, revisiting all 27 scene setups after random input, a fake-hub netcode test at 150 ms latency with jitter and 5% loss, and a scripted playthrough of the whole vacation as all six fighters, to both endings. In Chromium via Playwright from file://: a tour, the attract, an emulated touch-only phone, and a four-player Beach Match on two keyboard halves and two emulated controllers (navigator.getGamepads stubbed with standard-mapping pads). That run checks PlayStation and Xbox glyphs, Serve Cam in a live rally, every attract beat and every photo filter. No physical controller was tested. Also the engine\\'s tools/check.mjs, the AI Hub harness on 127.0.0.1 (4 scenarios), and screenshots and rig sheets for the art. TESTING-LOG.md lists every issue found.'],","+    ['Testing', 'One command (node test/run.mjs) that prints only failures and a count: 22 suites and 809 checks, all passing on the final run. Headless in Node with game.advance and game.debug: units (ball flight, rules, judge, data), AI-vs-AI match statistics, the vacation, shops, story, minigames, UI, attract, dev mode, saves, revisiting all 27 scene setups after random input, a fake-hub netcode test at 150 ms latency with jitter and 5% loss, and a scripted playthrough of the whole vacation as all six fighters, to both endings. In Chromium via Playwright from file://: a tour, the attract, an emulated touch-only phone, and a four-player Beach Match on two keyboard halves and two emulated controllers (navigator.getGamepads stubbed with standard-mapping pads). That run checks PlayStation and Xbox glyphs, Serve Cam in a live rally, every attract beat and every photo filter. No physical controller was tested. Also the engine\\'s tools/check.mjs, the AI Hub harness on 127.0.0.1 (4 scenarios), and screenshots and rig sheets for the art. TESTING-LOG.md lists every issue found.'],","     ['Research', 'No web research. Read the engine handoff (API card, guide, index, asset card), the sports kit, the engine source for the Humanoid, Dialog, audio, input and Shell, the AI Hub protocol README, client and harness checks, and the engine repository\\'s motion-capture catalogs. The source game was described from general knowledge, by the plan.'],","     ['Environment', 'Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown'],","     ['Model', 'Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh'],","-    ['Usage', 'Cost and tokens unknown (no meter was available to the model). By the system clock the build ran from 2026-11-03 22:54:53 (TASK.md\\'s start time) to @END@ when this text was last updated, @SPAN@.']","+    ['Usage', 'Cost and tokens unknown (no meter was available to the model). By the system clock the build ran from 2026-11-03 22:54:53 (TASK.md\\'s start time) to 2026-11-04 01:22:38 when this text was last updated, 2 h 27 min.']","   ],","   testing: [","     ['How many issues did testing catch?', '47 game issues, each listed in TESTING-LOG.md. Scripted tests caught 20, for example: rallies that never ended because the AI dug everything; a perfect player losing because the CPU spiked into the net; a starting partner never assigned; scene state carried from one visit to the next; Continue and Load crashing; Pool Hop\\'s beat clock; the attract missing input during fades. Screenshots and rig sheets caught 27, for example: the net seen edge-on; overlapping text and panels; tiny text in the engine\\'s HTML menus; two menu actions on one key for keyboard-half players; Serve Cam cutting off a player. Separately, 10 bugs in the tests themselves.'],"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453/TESTING-LOG.md","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-225453__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-225453/src/55-about.js"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G1P6EWxp1S6BpJxgH4